; SHORT WAVE DISRUPTORS, the core system (design 1.1, 2). SP1 shipped it empty with its name and
; flavour rows; SP2 adds the Mask of Many Faces menu and three of its modes' reactions - Drain,
; Stabilizer Override and Soulbind (each hidden, each on its own usage_group so no two share a round
; or a turn, memory lancer-tactics-reactions-and-usage). SP3 adds Entrap and Ensorcel, SP4 Neuro-Hijack.
;
; ORDER: the passive's menu first - it is the one action the card draws - then the modes in card order,
; then SP4's Neuro-Hijack, the core active (a PROTOCOL; its listener buff does the work).
;
; KEEP THIS KIT NON-TECH (design 2.1's trap): if it ever carries a tech action, every reaction on it is
; refused against tech-immune units (unit_action.gd:567-571, action_reaction.gd:107-110). SP5: icon.
[resource]
script = ExtResource("2_kit")
actions = Array[ExtResource("1_action")]([ExtResource("3_mask"), ExtResource("4_drain"), ExtResource("5_stab"), ExtResource("6_soul"), ExtResource("7_entrap"), ExtResource("8_hijack")])
is_trait = true
icon_override = ExtResource("9_icon")
